مرحلة 18 — دفع أولياء الأمور أونلاين (Paymob)
PHASE 18: ONLINE PARENT PAYMENTS
Uses PaymentProvider from Phase 17. Flag: parentPayments.
- Settings > الدفع الأونلاين: toggle each method independently: card, mobile wallet, Fawry reference (pay at a Fawry outlet), InstaPay. Availability depends on the merchant account, so each method has an enabled flag. If a method is not supported by the gateway account (for example InstaPay), offer a 'manual transfer' fallback: show the center's transfer details, let the parent upload a proof screenshot, and send it to a staff approval queue.
- Parent portal: open invoices list, pay one or several invoices, full or partial amount (minimum amount setting), method picker, summary with any gateway fee. Optional setting 'pass gateway fee to parent' (OFF by default and always shown clearly before payment).
- Flow: create a pending Payment attempt, redirect to hosted checkout (mock), and on return show a pending page. NEVER trust the return URL: only the verified webhook marks an invoice paid. Handle success, failure, pending (including Fawry reference with expiry and countdown), cancel, and duplicate webhooks. Idempotent so an invoice cannot be paid twice or over its remaining amount.
- On success: create the Payment (method and gateway transaction id), update the invoice, generate the receipt automatically (A5 and thermal formats), show a download button in the portal, notify the parent, and queue a WhatsApp receipt message (Phase 19).
- Staff screens: online payments list with status filters, transaction details, reconciliation view comparing gateway transactions to recorded payments with mismatches highlighted, and refund or void by accountant, admin or owner with a required reason and activity-log entry.
- Receptionist cannot edit online payments. Parents see only their own children's invoices.
Acceptance: success, failure, pending and duplicate-webhook scenarios all behave correctly on the mock; reconciliation finds a deliberately created mismatch.
مرحلة 19 — واتساب تلقائي (Cloud API)
PHASE 19: WHATSAPP CLOUD API AUTOMATION
Uses MessagingProvider from Phase 17. Flag: whatsappAutomation. Keep the wa.me manual flow as a fallback when automation is off.
- Settings > واتساب: provider status, phone number display, mode, sending limits, quiet hours (default no sends between 22:00 and 08:00), and an opt-in policy.
- Template manager: Meta requires pre-approved templates for messages the business starts. Map each internal template (absence, payment receipt, payment reminder, exam result, session reminder, monthly report) to a template name, language and ordered variables, with an approval status (معتمد / قيد المراجعة / مرفوض) and a preview. A message type without an approved template cannot be sent automatically. Free-form text is allowed only inside the 24-hour window after the parent last wrote to the center.
- Consent: track opt-in per parent (source, date, who recorded it) and honor opt-out keywords. Never send to a number without opt-in when automation is on.
- Queue: outbox items go through a sending queue with rate limiting, retries with exponential backoff, and permanent-failure handling. Extend statuses: queued, sent, delivered, read, failed (with error code and Arabic explanation).
- Status webhooks update the outbox through the Phase 17 handler. Show per-message status in the messages log and per-student last-contact info.
- Triggers (each with a setting: automatic, needs approval, or off): absence after attendance is saved (with configurable delay), payment receipt, payment reminders (Phase 21), exam results, monthly report.
- Cost tracking: count messages by category per month and let the center enter its own per-message rates to see an estimated monthly cost. Do not hard-code any prices.
- Messages log screen with filters, retry, and export (CSV module).
Acceptance: only approved templates are sent; opt-out blocks sending; statuses progress from queued to read on the mock; quiet hours defer sends.
مرحلة 20 — قفل اليومية (الخزنة)
PHASE 20: CASH REGISTER SHIFTS AND DAILY CLOSE
Flag: cashRegister.
- Open shift: cashier, opening float, start time. Only one open shift per cashier. Every cash payment, cash expense and cash settlement is attached to the open shift; non-cash methods (wallet, card, transfer, online) are totaled separately by method and never counted as cash in the drawer.
- Expected cash = opening float + cash payments - cash expenses/settlements paid out. Show a live running summary during the shift.
- Close shift: the cashier counts the drawer (optional denomination counter for 200, 100, 50, 20, 10, 5, 1 EGP and coins) and enters the actual cash. The system shows the variance (short or over). A configurable tolerance; beyond it a reason is required and a manager approval is needed.
- Locking: once closed, the shift's payments and expenses become immutable. Corrections are made only by an adjustment entry with a reason, linked to the original (never by editing).
- Reports: end-of-shift report (A4 and 80mm), daily totals across shifts, per-cashier variance history, per-method totals. CSV export.
- Handover: closing a shift can start the next cashier's shift with the opening float carried over.
- Alerts: shift open for more than 24 hours; repeated variances for the same cashier.
- Permissions: receptionist and accountant open and close their own shift; owner and admin approve variances and may reopen a closed shift with a reason; teachers have no access.
Acceptance: expected vs counted calculation is correct; non-cash is excluded; closed shifts cannot be edited; adjustments are traceable.
مرحلة 21 — تذكيرات الدفع التلقائية بجدول
PHASE 21: AUTOMATIC PAYMENT REMINDER SCHEDULE
Flag: autoReminders. Uses the job scheduler and the WhatsApp/outbox layer.
- Rules editor in Settings: an ordered list of steps relative to the invoice due date, for example -2 days, due day, +3, +7, +14. Each step has a channel (parent portal notification, WhatsApp, or both), a template, and an on/off switch. Provide a sensible default schedule and a reset button.
- Stop conditions: invoice paid, installment plan covers it, student on hold, or an active promise-to-pay date. Maximum reminders per invoice. Respect quiet hours and parent opt-out.
- Escalation: at the last step create a task for staff (a follow-up list on the dashboard) instead of another message.
- Promise to pay: staff record a promised date and note; reminders pause until that date.
- Daily job: idempotent (never sends the same step twice for an invoice), logs every decision (sent, skipped and why), and handles invoices created or changed after the schedule started.
- Screens: upcoming reminders calendar, per-student reminder history, pause or resume per student, and a dry-run preview showing what would be sent today.
Acceptance: running the job twice sends nothing twice; a paid invoice stops reminders; the dry run matches what is actually sent.
